WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.820
We've had an incredible 24 hours in the United
States.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:09.350
I want to start today with huge news out of
Minneapolis where the other three officers,

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:14.670
as they are known, involved in the death of
Jorge Floyd, have now been charged.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:20.699
And the charges against Derek Schavan have
been upgraded from third degree murder to

00:00:20.699 --> 00:00:22.239
second degree murder.

00:00:22.239 --> 00:00:23.289
A lot to discuss.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:29.609
So starting off with reminder, Derek Schavan
is the officer in the viral video that spurred

00:00:29.609 --> 00:00:33.130
the national and even global protests.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:38.950
The officer putting his knee to George Floyd's
neck for many minutes before George George

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:40.060
Floyd ultimately died.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:44.410
The three officers visible in the video sort
of standing around as this happens, have now

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:49.840
been charged with aiding and abetting second
degree murder and aiding and abetting second

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:55.810
degree manslaughter, second degree murder,
and aiding and abetting second degree murder,

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:59.350
punishable by up to 40 years in prison.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.509
Manslaughter, aiding and abetting manslaughter
punishable by up to 10 years in prison.

00:01:04.509 --> 00:01:06.789
Now, let's talk about the Derek Schavan charges.

00:01:06.789 --> 00:01:09.840
And this is there's a lot of detail here that's
important.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:15.229
The original charges against Derek Schavan
were third degree murder and second degree

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:17.060
manslaughter.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.790
The murder charge has now been upgraded to
second degree murder.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:27.850
This is very important because second degree
murder carries with it.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:34.759
Number one, a much more serious potential
sentence, but also, number two, potentially

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:39.810
a more difficult to prove case for the prosecution
in a sense.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:45.569
Sort of maybe, except that the third degree
murder charges, when you look at the statute,

00:01:45.569 --> 00:01:48.499
also may not have been the right ones for
the situation.

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:51.719
So, again, we've got to look at what the statutes
say.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:59.709
In Minnesota, a third degree murder charge
is defined as, quote, whoever without intent

00:01:59.709 --> 00:02:04.579
to effect the death of any person, meaning
without deliberately trying to kill someone

00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:12.190
causes the death of another by perpetrating
an act eminently dangerous to others and evincing

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:18.110
a depraved mind not or evincing a depraved
mind and evincing a depraved mind without

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:22.180
regard for human life is guilty of murder
in the third degree.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.690
So this is from the twenty nineteen Minnesota
statutes.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:34.890
And what Schavan did would be very tough to
prove in a court of law as what's called a

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.270
depraved mind murder.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:43.650
So you can make the case not that the charge
should be second degree versus third degree

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:48.910
based on the severity, so to speak, of what
Derek Schavan is accused of doing.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:55.500
But because the third degree murder statute
includes this depraved mind component.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.170
So instead, we have second degree murder here.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:05.860
There are two types of second degree murder
in Minnesota statutes, intentional and unintentional.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:13.180
If sharpens restraint of George Floyd caused
Floyd's death, he could be guilty of unintentional

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:17.780
second degree murder even if he was not trying
to kill George Floyd.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:23.830
It would be very difficult to prove in a court
of law based on what we've seen, that Schavan

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.600
was trying to kill George Floyd.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:34.990
It seems as though unintentional second degree
murder is the statute under which George Floyds

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.840
death would fall.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.610
From the perspective of Derek Chauvin's actions,
now, there's one more analysis here about

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:42.610
this.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.980
That's less about what you can prove, but
more about what Schavan is likely to plead

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:47.980
down to.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:52.740
So let me kind of frame this up for you in
a different way.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:58.400
If this goes to trial, I think it's going
to be tough, but not impossible to get a guilty

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.090
verdict against Derek Schavan.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:02.840
That has nothing to do with my opinion about
what went down.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.070
It is merely my understanding of how these
trials often work and what the law is.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.480
So bear with me here.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:14.480
We have two autopsies that were done of George
Floyd so far that that I've read in one of

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.200
those autopsies.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.579
The cause of death is not alone.

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:25.090
The actions of Derek Schavan, the cause of
death says it was not asphyxiation by Derek

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:32.040
Schavan and it was the restraint used by Derek
Schavan, combined with preexisting medical

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.940
conditions and possible intoxication.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:36.490
Now, you and I may think that that's B.S.

00:04:36.490 --> 00:04:40.980
And indeed, there's a second autopsy which
says something very different, which says

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:47.240
that the death was indeed caused by asphyxiation
as a result of Derek Chauvin's actions.

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:53.720
But my point is, if this goes to trial, a
good defense attorney, which Derek Schavan

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.830
will certainly have, is very much able to
introduce.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:03.431
Reasonable doubt about whether Chauvin's actions
definitely are the cause of George Floyds

00:05:03.431 --> 00:05:08.620
death by focusing on the one autopsy that
says, you know, there were preexisting medical

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.840
conditions that were a factor, possible intoxication
and restraint.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:18.740
You bring in some medical examiners that they'll
find and say, Doctor, whoever given this autopsy,

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:26.031
is it possible that absent George Floyds medical
conditions and possible intoxication, that

00:05:26.031 --> 00:05:30.000
he could have survived the way that he was
restrained by Derek Schavan?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.240
Yes, counsel, that's possible.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:38.370
So you and I both understand that this is
apparently B.S., but you would then have a

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:44.560
fight, a legal fight where the defense is
introducing doubt and the prosecution is saying,

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:46.090
well, we have a different autopsy.

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:50.730
This OP Topsy does say that George Floyd was
asphyxiated by Derek Schavan.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:51.790
But it becomes a fight.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.530
And remember, you only need reasonable doubt
to acquit.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:06:00.480
The standard of evidence in a civil trial
may well be a preponderance of evidence.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:05.160
Does it seem like 51 percent of the evidence
points to Derek Chauvin's responsibility?

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.410
In a criminal trial, you need only introduce
reasonable doubt.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:12.820
So this gets me back to the reason for moving
from third degree murder to second degree

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:13.820
murder.

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:19.290
Is the idea that you go to a second degree
murder charge because it carries a higher

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:27.050
penalty so that you increase the desire from
Derek Schavan to plead to something smaller

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:32.840
to avoid a trial altogether, which may or
may not go well for the prosecution.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:37.450
That's another possibility as to why you would
have seen an elevated charge from third degree

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:39.030
murder to second degree murder.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:43.970
Needless to say, it is correct to elevate
the charge to second degree murder based on

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:46.350
our reading of the Minnesota statutes.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:51.200
And it is a good thing that the other officers
have been charged and all were brought in

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.200
yesterday.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:55.060
This is going to be this is going to be a
very long thing in.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:07:02.470
By every indication, this will not be resolved
for far longer than the current protests are

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.520
likely to go.

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:08.110
So we've got to really buckle in and realize
that this is going to be a long process.

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.150
Speedy trial.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.221
OK, it is still going to be a long and protracted
process.

